# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository (stable diffs, and the
# GitHub Actions bash steps never see stray CRLF / \r).
#
# Why it matters: release.yml's `run:` blocks execute as bash on the ubuntu runner. A CRLF
# blob makes every line end in \r and bash fails with "$'\r': command not found" — a break
# that is invisible in the repo and only shows up on release day.
#
# This currently changes NOTHING: `git add --renormalize` moved not a single blob, because
# core.autocrlf=true on this machine was already converting CRLF to LF on commit. The rule is
# here so the guarantee does not depend on one machine's git config. Matches the checklist
# mods, whose pipeline this one is copied from.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: no EOL normalization, no textual diff.
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.xcf binary
